<title>USA: Court approves Comptronix sale.</title>
<headline>Court approves Comptronix sale.</headline>
<dateline>BRENTWOOD, Tenn. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Comptronix Corp said on Thursday that the U.S. Bankruptcy Court for the Middle District of Tennessee has approved the sale of substantially all of its assets to Sanmina Corp.</p>
<p>Comptronix agreed to sell the assets to Sanmina for $20 million to $22 million in cash, depending upon a formula outlined in the contract between the two companies, the company said in a September 20 statement.</p>
<p>Consummation of the deal is expected to take place on November 1, 1996, the company said.</p>
</text>
